  "final_message": "`service2.compute_fee(1000, \"gold\")` returns **480**. Running it with Python gives the same result.\n\n`compute_fee` imports from only two modules, `pricing` and `discounts`:\n\n1. `pricing.base_fee(1000)` = 500 + 1000 // 10 = **600**\n2. `discounts.apply_discount(600, \"gold\")` applies the gold rate of 20%: 600 \u2212 (600 \u00d7 20) // 100 = 600 \u2212 120 = **480**\n\nNothing imports `decoy_tax.py` or `decoy_shipping.py`, so they don't affect the result. `decoy_tax.py` also has a `TIERS` table where gold is 25%, but it isn't used here.\n\nANSWER: 480",
